        "problem": "Consider the equation ${x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+26{x}^{2}+50x+25=0.$ Given that $x=-1$ is a solution of multiplicity $2,$ find the remaining solutions.",
        "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)={x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+26{x}^{2}+50x+25.$ Since ${x}_{1,2}=-1$ is a root of multiplicity $2,$ according to the factor theorem, \n\n$$\n(x+1)^{2}={x}^{2}+2x+1\n$$\n\nis a factor of $f(x).$ \n\nNow, we can use long division to find the quotient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+25 \\\\  & {x}^{2}+2x+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+26{x}^{2}+50x+25\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,25{x}^{2}+50x+25 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{25{x}^{2}+50x+25}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $f(x)=({x}^{2}+2x+1)({x}^{2}+25).$\n\nTo find the remaining two roots, we solve ${x}^{2}+25=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-25 \\\\ x & =\\pm 5\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to our original equation are $x=-1,\\,-1,\\,\\pm 5\\text{i}.$",
